<!--
  datamodel="sce-static" (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15, "Saving and
  restoring"): an `<invoke>` the HOST runs is part of what a machine is doing,
  and a saved machine that left it out would restore into a state that says
  "working" with nobody working.

  `working` hands a job to the host: the invoke carries a typed `<param>` read
  from the machine's fields (`job`, `label`), an inline `<content>`, a `src`,
  and a deadline (`_sce_deadline_ms`, which the engine keeps rather than handing
  to the host). The host answers later, with `done.invoke.h` or `error.invoke.h`,
  or the deadline does:

    done.invoke.h    leaves `working` for `after`, and records a 1 in `seen`
    error.invoke.h   leaves `working` for `failed`, and records a 2
    leave            leaves `working` for `idle`, which cancels the invocation

  The `<param>`s are written in the alphabetical order of their names, which is
  not a style choice. The request's `event_data` is a JSON object whose keys come
  out in the order each backend builds them — the document's order on Kotlin,
  alphabetical on Rust (measured 2026-10-02) — and a saved state holds that text
  as it was, one text for both backends to write and read. In this order the two
  agree; the difference itself is not hidden by it, only kept out of a test that
  is about something else.

  `seen` is a decimal number that grows a digit for each such event, so it says
  WHICH arrived and in what order, as `trace` does in static_timers.scxml: 1 is
  a completion, 2 a failure, 12 a completion and then a failure.

  A restore starts the invocation again from the request it was saved with
  (`restarted`, a new token, the deadline it had left) and never evaluates the
  element a second time: `job` and `label` may have changed since the start, and
  the host is owed the values the document sent.

  Generated with the invoker declaration naming the type x-sce-host
  (scripts/regen_host_processor.sh and scripts/regen_host_processor_kotlin.sh
  name the flag; an XML comment cannot spell a double hyphen).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0" initial="idle" datamodel="sce-static"
       name="statechart_static_host_invoke">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="job" sce:type="uint32" expr="7"/>
    <data id="label" sce:type="string" expr="'report'"/>
    <data id="seen" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
  </datamodel>

  <state id="idle">
    <transition event="bump">
      <assign location="job" expr="job + 1"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="start" target="working"/>
  </state>

  <state id="working">
    <invoke type="x-sce-host" id="h" src="job://report">
      <param name="_sce_deadline_ms" expr="5000"/>
      <param name="job" expr="job"/>
      <param name="label" expr="label"/>
      <content>payload</content>
    </invoke>
    <transition event="bump">
      <assign location="job" expr="job + 1"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="done.invoke.h" target="after">
      <assign location="seen" expr="seen * 10 + 1"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.invoke.h" target="failed">
      <assign location="seen" expr="seen * 10 + 2"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="leave" target="idle"/>
  </state>

  <state id="after"/>
  <state id="failed"/>
</scxml>
